DATA LICENCE — data/ca-math/
============================

The code in this repository is Apache-2.0 (see LICENSE). The data is not, and the
boundary matters, because the two carry different obligations.

Everything under `data/ca-math/` is a filtered derivative of the Learning Commons
Knowledge Graph public JSONL export, v1.11.0, and travels under the licence its source
records carry:

    Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Each record retains its own `license` and `attributionStatement` fields. Where a record's
own attribution string differs from the general statement below, THE RECORD'S OWN STRING
GOVERNS. There is no single correct attribution line for this dataset: the strings vary by
jurisdiction and by node type, and four distinct ones touch the California mathematics
vertical alone.

General statement, as published in the source data:

    "Knowledge Graph is provided by Learning Commons under the CC BY-4.0 license.
     Learning Commons received state standards and written permission under CC BY-4.0
     from 1EdTech."

Per-layer provenance is in NOTICE.


A rider that is easy to miss
----------------------------

The Common Core State Standards statement text inside these records is separately
licensed by NGA Center and CCSSO under a bespoke public licence that is NOT Creative
Commons and is narrower than CC BY 4.0 in two ways:

  * it carries a purpose limitation — use must support the Common Core State Standards
    Initiative;
  * it mandates this notice:

        © 2010 National Governors Association Center for Best Practices (NGA Center) and
        Council of Chief State School Officers (CCSSO). All rights reserved.

Do not relabel CCSS statement text as CC BY 4.0 on the strength of the surrounding
record's licence field. The container and the contents are licensed by different parties.


What is deliberately absent
---------------------------

`data/raw/` is not distributed here. It is the upstream Learning Commons export
(approximately 812 MB), and it is not needed: `data/ca-math/` is the filtered product and
the ingest builds the store from it directly.

    python -m k12_toolkit.ingest --source data/ca-math --db data/standards.db

The built SQLite store is a derived artifact and is not tracked. Rebuild it rather than
copying it, so that what you query is what this repository actually contains.


Licences expire
---------------

Every licence verdict this project rests on carries the date it was checked. That is not
bookkeeping. Two grants relied on by adjacent open-education projects were withdrawn
inside six months during 2026, and third-party indexes went on publishing the old answer
afterwards. If you are depending on this file long after the date in its git history,
re-check the source rather than trusting the copy in front of you.
